    "lawCode": "Add Art 44-C §§1430 - 1432, Gen Bus L",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6955A\n\nSPONSOR: GOUNARDES\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to establishing\nthe artificial intelligence training data transparency act\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo provide the public with information regarding the data used to train\ncertain artificial intelligence models\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one describes the amendment to the General Business Law\n\nSubsection 1430 provides a short title Subsection 1431 provides defi-\nnitions\n\nSubsection 1432 describes the data that must be disclosed when used to\ntrain generative artificial intelligence systems or services\n\nSection two establishes the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nInspired by a law in California, this legislation is designed to promote\ntransparency and accountability in the development and deployment of\ngenerative artificial intelligence models. As AI continues to influence\na wide range of industries, understanding the data used to train these\nmodels is crucial for ensuring that they are developed ethically,\nresponsibly, and in a manner that protects public interests. By requir-\ning developers to provide documentation detailing the datasets used to\ntrain their AI systems, the bill ensures we are able to understand what\ndata underpins their functionality. This requirement will help identify\nany biases, inaccuracies, or ethical concerns in the training data that\nmay impact the performance and fairness of AI models, all while giving\nconsumers, regulators, and stakeholders the tools to better assess and\nengage with these technologies.\n\nThis bill provides New Yorkers with valuable insight about how data is\nused to train the increasingly powerful AI models they interact with on\na day to day basis and which have come to power the innovation economy.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2025: Referred to Internet and Technology\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
